+/* Copyright 2026 The Sunshine OS contributors
+ * Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
+ * found in the LICENSE file.
+ *
+ * This stylesheet declares no colour, and that is deliberate rather than an
+ * omission. Two reasons, either of which would be enough.
+ *
+ * First, it cannot: chrome://theme is not reachable from a chrome-untrusted://
+ * origin, whose style-src permits chrome-untrusted://resources,
+ * chrome-untrusted://theme and 'self' (ui/webui/webui_util.cc,
+ * SetJSModuleDefaults). Reaching for a colour here would mean either adding a
+ * theme source to an untrusted origin or writing a literal, and
+ * docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM_CONTRACT.md section 2.3 is explicit that a colour that
+ * escapes the theme must fail visibly rather than be papered over with a
+ * fallback.
+ *
+ * Second, it should not. Giving user-authored content the browser's own
+ * surface palette would let a document imitate the privileged shell that
+ * embeds it, which is the confusion the shell/frame split exists to prevent.
+ * The user agent's colours, under the color-scheme this page declares, are the
+ * honest ones for content that is not Sunshine's.
+ *
+ * What is left is layout, in rem, on the section 6.2 scale. */
+
+body {
+  margin: 0;
+}
+
+#placeholder {
+  font-size: 0.875rem;
+  line-height: 1.43;
+  margin: 0;
+  padding: 1rem;
+}
+
+/* A document is arbitrary markup and may be wider than the frame. It scrolls
+ * inside the frame rather than being rewritten to fit: pagination and fitting
+ * are presentation, and the stored document is never altered for either
+ * (DOC-4). */
+#content {
+  font-size: 1rem;
+  line-height: 1.5;
+  overflow-x: auto;
+  padding: 1rem;
+}
